responses.text:
Given a figure, we need to color each hexagon either red, green or yellow in such a way that the sides of adjacent hexagons do not have the same colour. Step 1: Identify pairs of adjacent hexagons. Step 2: Create a table to keep track of pairs of hexagons joined at an edge, based on the character Grmy - green, red, yellow.

Step 3: Start by coloring the first hexagon. Since this hexagon is already colored, we assume it's red. That is, the LONDO hexagon is red.

Step 4: We'll color the hexagon to the immediate left - LONDO-RE - red. Now it has two neighbors, RED with the LONDO hexagon and LONDO-RE with the immediately previously colored hexagon (which is red, so we'll call this line RED with OLD).

Step 5: Next is the hexagon to the immediate left of the previously colored RED - RED-OLD-OLD. It has to be colored a different color to RED-OLD, and the possibilities we have are YEL (green) and GR (red or yellow) (or, we can repeat colors in this hexagon, but since it doesn't have yellow, we'll just stick to GR+YEL). If we colored the HEXAGON NEXT TO RED with GR, it will have to be GR-OLD-YEL-OLD because it has to be GREEN and the two previous ones are RED and GR. If we colored it with YEL we'll have YEL-OLD-RED-HALF.

Step 6: The third hexagon to the left of the previously coloured one, GR-RED-YEL will have to be GR-RED+BET. The other side is YELLOW again. If we put YELLOW-RED on the other side, we can't use the same color twice, so GR-RED-LIN has to be GR-RED-YEL or GR-RED+COL, which corresponds to GR and YEL on the other sides. If we put GR-OLD-BET, the other side must be GR+OLD along with YEL. That means we can't draw GR+OLD-YEL_hexagonBET because that color would be repeated twice.

Step 7: Proceed with the same puzzle for the hexagon to the right of the previously colored hexagon, GR-BES. We have GR-based-BETREV. If we use the color GR, the previous side has to be GR-OLD+OLD. Then the next side has to be GR and the final color has to be YEL+OLD along with GR. We can't draw this as a GR-BETREV case, so we have GR-BETREV-BET and GRREV-BETREV_BET cases.

[asy]   unitsize(15);
for(int a = 0; a <= 8; ++a) {
draw((a,0)--(a+1,0));
}

for(int[] x = {-5, 0, 5}; lengthof(x) <= 8; ++x) {
draw((x[0],0)--(x[1],0));
}

path Hex = (x[1], 0)--(x[2],3.464)--(x[4], 0)--(x[5], 3.464)--(x[7],0)--(x[6],3.464)--(x[1],0)--cycle;
draw(Hex);
draw(shift((x[2], 3.464))*Hex);
draw(shift((x[4], 0))*Hex);
draw(shift((x[7],0))*Hex);
draw(shift((x[6], 3.464))*Hex);
draw(shift((x[5], 3.464))*Hex);
draw(shift((0, 3.464))*Hex);
[/asy] Compile the WAYS. Answer is containing copies of those figures labeled with the same color.
